3. That your company has utilised substandard construction materials in violation of Clause 7 of the JDA, including M-20 grade concrete instead of the mandated M-30, and Fe-415 grade steel instead of Fe-500D, thereby compromising structural integrity of the buildings.

4. That Rs. 5,75,00,000/- of the funds received remain unaccounted for, and our client has reason to believe that a sum of Rs. 2,80,00,000/- was diverted to a personal bank account of your Managing Director.

5. That despite the Supplementary Agreement dated 18.10.2023, no additional investment of Rs. 8,00,00,000/- as committed therein has been made. No structural audit by a Grade-A auditor has been conducted. No escrow account has been opened.

Our client hereby demands:
(a) Payment of Rs. 20,25,00,000/- being the total amount paid, with interest at 18% per annum;
(b) Return of vacant, peaceful possession of the Said Property;
(c) Payment of Rs. 2,00,00,000/- as penalty under Clause 9.1;
(d) Compensation of Rs. 30,00,00,000/- towards loss of opportunity and diminution in land value;

You are called upon to comply within 30 days, failing which our client shall be constrained to initiate appropriate civil and criminal proceedings.

Sd/- Advocate Priya Mehta
M/s Mehta & Associates
